  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Attendance may vary, and the shared notes, score-change record, and approved practice recordings are available without requiring an additional rehearsal.\", \"decision\": \"How should an absent singer catch up?\", \"goal\": \"Make rehearsals easy to attend and prepare for while helping singers use shared rehearsal time effectively.\", \"problem\": \"A community choir is preparing a small program through a series of rehearsals. It has a conductor, willing section leaders, a booking organizer, numbered scores that members may use, and shared practice recordings. The rehearsal room has movable chairs and enough space for short sectional work. Members have varied experience and availability. Musical direction remains with the conductor, and each routine below can operate within any agreed rehearsal schedule.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nAbsent singers receive the rehearsal notes and use the linked change record and recordings before returning. The same concise package lets each person catch up independently at a time compatible with their other commitments.\nEach absent singer asks a designated section partner for a brief walkthrough of the notes and linked practice materials. A familiar peer can explain which changes mattered most and clarify questions before the singer rejoins the group.\nSection leaders send absent singers a short prioritized message linking the rehearsal notes, changed markings, and relevant recordings. Catch-up begins with the most important work for that voice part while preserving access to the complete shared record."
    }
  ],
